@using PullbackStrategyLab.Web.Shell
@model LabStatusView
@*
    The band across the top of every screen. It spans the whole page because the position cap
    and the total risk are account-wide rather than per side.

    Every figure the lab does not produce yet renders as a dash and the checkpoint that will
    produce it, never as a zero. A zero reads as "none open" where the truth is "positions are
    not a thing yet".
*@
@if (!Model.Reachable)
{
    <p class="down">The read surface is not answering: @Model.Unreachable. The pages render; the figures do not.</p>
}

@*
    The store being at a version other than the build's is stated outright rather than left to be
    read off the two numbers in the band. A stage that needs a column the store has not got fails
    with a message naming the column, and every night it fails is a night that produces nothing.
*@
@if (Model.SchemaMismatch && !Model.StoreAhead)
{
    <p class="down">
        The store is at schema @Model.SchemaVersion and this build needs @Model.SchemaVersionExpected.
        Stages that read a column the store has not got will fail. Run <code>tools/migrate</code>, then
        rerun the night's stages for their own date.
    </p>
}
@if (Model.StoreAhead)
{
    @* The other direction, and it needs the other act. A store ahead of the build means an older
       binary is reading columns whose meaning has moved, so a migration is not owed and running one
       would not help. The checkout is what has to change. Program.WhyTheStoreCannotBeRead already
       says this; until 4.2 the band collapsed both directions into one label and sent the operator
       to run a migration that was not owed. *@
    <p class="down">
        The store is at schema @Model.SchemaVersion and this build was written against
        @Model.SchemaVersionExpected, so the store is <b>ahead</b> of the build reading it. Do not run
        <code>tools/migrate</code>: it has nothing to apply. This checkout is older than the store and
        is what has to change.
    </p>
}

<div class="band">
    <div><b>Session</b>@Model.SessionText</div>
    <div><b>Store</b>@Model.StoreText</div>
    <div><b>Last run</b>@Model.LastRunText</div>
    <div><b>Calls today</b>@Model.CallsText</div>
    <div><b>Mood</b>@(Model.MarketMood ?? LabStatusView.Awaiting("2.5"))</div>
    <div><b>Open</b>@(Model.PositionsOpen?.ToString() ?? LabStatusView.Awaiting("4.7"))</div>
    <div><b>Risk at stake</b>@(Model.RiskAtStake?.ToString("0.00'%'") ?? LabStatusView.Awaiting("4.7"))</div>
</div>
